play_title; BeadsBackend at beads_backend.py:593 not mentioned in item\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nChanges from snapshot: None \u2014 all conditions confirmed AVAILABLE through direct codebase research.\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-22)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP2 \u2014 Medium priority infrastructure quality item. No active regression observed; preventative measure.\\nEffort: Low \u2014 approximately 25 lines of test code following existing pattern at `test_rendering.py:51-83`. No new imports, no production code changes. Estimated implementation: under 30 minutes.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blast radius: 1 file (`test_rendering.py`, test-only addition)\\n- Production code: unchanged\\n- Test suite: one new parametrized test class/function\\n- CI runtime: minimal addition (milliseconds per backend instance)\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Completes parity between `render_groomed_section` and `section_display_title` cross-backend test coverage\\n- Creates a regression safety net: if any backend deviates from canonical rendering delegation, CI catches it immediately\\n- Lowers future maintenance risk when adding new backends \u2014 the new backend must pass the consistency test or fail CI\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen called with the same `key` and `groomed_date` arguments, all backends return the same value as `_rendering.section_display_title(key, groomed_date)`:\\n- `GitHubBackend.section_display_title(key, d)` == canonical output\\n- `SQLiteBackend.section_display_title(key, d)` == canonical output\\n- `InMemoryBackend.section_display_title(key, d)` == canonical output\\n- `BeadsBackend.section_display_title(key, d)` == canonical output\\n\\nFailure state (what the test prevents): a backend silently diverging from the canonical implementation while CI passes.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A parametrized test in `backlog_core/tests/test_rendering.py` calls `backend.section_display_title(key, groomed_date)`